1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:05,383
Connect a coding assistant with a personal, limited and revocable access token.

2
00:00:06,253 --> 00:00:18,214
Open Integrations and create an access token. Give it a recognisable name and an expiry date. Access stays limited to your own Minutrel data, even for an administrator.

3
00:00:19,287 --> 00:00:30,543
Choose whether the assistant can read your projects, time and work notes, or suggest private drafts. Timer control is a separate permission and is not enabled by default.

4
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:45,972
Store the token privately in MINUTREL_MCP_TOKEN. Set up my assistant shows configurations for Codex and Claude Code using the team MCP endpoint. Keep the secret out of your source repository.

5
00:00:47,053 --> 00:00:57,868
The access list shows names and expiry dates. Revoke a token to stop its access. The assistant’s proposed notes remain private drafts until you review them.

6
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:13,409
An administrator can separately configure Ollama, vLLM or Claude for summary drafting. That needs a real configured provider and your consent to send the selected notes. Time tracking works without it.

7
00:01:14,953 --> 00:01:19,369
Your permissions decide the access. Your review decides what gets shared.
